KayaMo is a Personal Growth OS (see `Mus_Build_Source_of_Truth.md`). PWA first,
Capacitor wrap for Android/iOS. Solo developer. First market: Philippines.
Bundle ID `ph.kayamo.app`. AI companion is named Mus.

## Monorepo layout — put code in the right place
- `apps/pwa`    — mobile-first user app. Routes, nav chrome, thin glue only.
- `apps/web`    — desktop review shell. Keyboard-first, data-dense.
- `apps/admin`  — internal tools, auth-gated, never public.
- `apps/mobile` — Capacitor shell. Native code only, zero business logic.
- `packages/features` — screen logic, data hooks, layout-neutral components.
- `packages/db` `core` `food` `ai` `offline` `ui` — all shared logic.

apps/pwa is mobile-first and thumb-driven. apps/web is desktop,
keyboard-first, data-dense. Neither contains business logic — that
lives in packages/features. A screen implemented twice is a bug.

Packages never import from apps. Apps never duplicate package logic.
If a formula or a resolver appears inside `apps/`, that is a bug.

## Non-negotiable
- Never call an LLM without a Zod schema on the output.
- Never write nutrition data without `source` and `confidence`.
- The LLM extracts text and quantities. Nutrition numbers come from the
  resolver cascade in @kayamo/food, never from the model.
- Every AI-created entry is editable by the user. Mus proposes; the user confirms.
- Stored data is not automatically AI-readable.
- Offline first: writes go to IndexedDB via @kayamo/offline, then sync.
- Store UTC, render in the user's timezone. Respect their custom day
  boundary (night shift) — never assume midnight.
- All money in PHP.
- Calorie floors (1200F / 1500M) are enforced in code, not prompts.
- Banned vocabulary anywhere in prompts or UI copy: cheat, guilty, earned,
  burn it off, bad food, sinful.
- Health data never appears in logs or error reports.
- Never modify a test to make it pass. Fix the code, or tell me the test
  is wrong and why.

## Conventions
- pnpm workspaces + turbo. TypeScript strict. No `any`.
- The service-role Supabase client is never imported into a "use client" file.
- All LLM calls route through @kayamo/ai `router.ts`.
- One chapter per commit. See chapter numbering below.

## Chapter numbering — one system only
`chNN` in a commit message ALWAYS refers to `docs/build/`. It NEVER refers
to Mus source-of-truth phase numbers. Build-guide ch20 is the weekly
check-in; ch23 is the progression engine; ch24 links training to
nutrition. If work comes from the Mus SoT instead, prefix the commit
`mus:` and name the feature — never a bare number.
Before starting any chapter, read `docs/build/README.md` and confirm the
number against the checklist there.
